## Objective
--------------
Understand how web applications receive information through URL parameters.
------------------
## Topics Covered
------------------
- URL Structure
- Query Parameters
- Resource Identification
- Search Parameters
- Pagination
- Language Parameters
--------------------
## Parameters Studied

?id=

?q=

?page=

&lang=

&view=

## Practical Understanding
-------------------------
- Identified resources using ID parameters
- Understood search queries in URLs
- Recognised pagination parameters
- Analysed language parameters
- Read URLs as structured requests instead of random text
----------------------------
## Key Learning

Different URL parameters provide different instructions to the web application.

Examples:

id = object identifier

q = search query

page = page number

lang = language

view = content to display
